I would like to know what would be a large enough sample size to detect epistasis QTLs with sufficient power and discriminate between signal and noise.

It depends on the strength of the underlying effects.

> Are the above steps sufficient or would I need to perform additional steps to contol for type I errors?

I prefer to formulate the problem as variable/model selection rather than hypothesis testing, and my basic recommended approach is that in stepwiseqtl(), as described in Manichaikul et al. (2009) A model selection approach for the identification of quantitative trait loci in experimental crosses, allowing epistasis.Genetics <http://www.genetics.org/> 181:1077-1086

karl

