In-Reply-To: <SB5Jsk9IIbE.OrNLb7WRcZEJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
References: <SB5Jsk9IIbE.OrNLb7WRcZEJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rqtl-disc/c/SB5Jsk9IIbE/m/N5FTeFC3GbEJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The function c.cross() currently works only to combine crosses of the same type (e.g., both F2), or to combine backcrosses and intercrosses.

The simplest approach to combine the two studies would be to just add the LOD curves.

karl

